  "id": "5878c3a8-9b4f-5c06-8311-81b99fd556bd",
  "slug": "dry-brine-turkey",
  "name": "Dry Brine Turkey",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "This dry brine turkey recipe uses a simple salt rub to get a perfectly seasoned, juicy turkey with crispy skin. An easy get-ahead method for Thanksgiving.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Gather the ingredients."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Pat turkey dry with paper towels. Season inside and outside of turkey with kosher salt, focusing on breast and thighs. Place turkey, breast-side up, in the roasting pan and cover with plastic wrap. Refrigerate turkey for about 2 days."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Flip turkey breast-side down, cover with plastic wrap, and refrigerate for about 1 more day."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Remove plastic wrap and place turkey on a rack over a baking sheet the night before you plan to roast. Allow turkey to air-dry in the refrigerator for at least 8 hours. This step helps the skin crisp beautifully during roasting."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Bring turkey to room temperature, 1 to 2 hours; pat dry with paper towels. Season turkey with black pepper and place onion and celery in the cavity."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Preheat oven to 425 degrees F (220 degrees C). Place turkey, breast-side down, in a roasting pan."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Roast in the preheated oven until skin is golden, about 30 minutes. Remove turkey from oven and flip to breast-side up. Reduce oven temperature to 325 degrees F (165 degrees C); continue roasting until an instant-read thermometer inserted into the thickest part of the thigh reads 165 degrees F (74 degrees C), about 2 hours."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Transfer turkey to a large platter and loosely tent with aluminum foil; allow turkey to rest about 30 minutes before carving."
    }
  ],
